{"kind":"request","text":"Prepare the failed-claim register packet for one hosted Worker\n\nScope: the deployment half of parent 8a8902f3, after source 12a718fe landed at 28839920. I deployed 28839920 to dap-grow, dap-lending and dap-demo at 00:01 EST on 5 November with --keep-vars; every Worker accepts the failed-claim cohort for new scopes now, but no register on it exists. The parent's acceptance needs a Register 26 room created through the real commands, `dap install` and the Page offer using it by default, an actual one-hour token, and a clone refused after that hour.\n\nPrepare the packet, as for the G3b binding packet (1bb63a2f): a reviewed notes/implementation record plus the exact configuration change, and nothing deployed.\n1. Choose one hosted Worker with a repository host, and say why. Prefer the Worker whose live rooms are fewest and whose Page offer the parent names. Read its live registers and rooms from operator records and the scope-index census, read-only.\n2. Write the Wrangler change for that Worker: the planned Register 26 as REGISTER_SCOPE, every earlier register whose rooms still need children in INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES, and the host setting's registerScope, with a placeholder for the planned ID. Follow docs/deploy.md \"Keep existing rooms able to create children\".\n3. Write the planner's procedure: plan from a new private home with `dap install --plan \u003curl\u003e --host \u003chost\u003e --namespace \u003cns\u003e`, fill the placeholder, deploy, and install within the plan's 14 minutes; then the health and existing-room checks; then the scratch room, the token and the post-hour clone refusal. Include the rollback.\n4. Show with the production parsers that the filled configuration is accepted and that a missing old root is refused.\n\nThe plan's 14-minute window means the configuration commit cannot be reviewed between plan and install. So review the packet with the placeholder, and I deploy the filled copy; the record of the filled values lands afterwards under its own review.\n\nOrder: next, before plan 035 M1–M2 source work, because it closes a parent and needs no derive edits. O4 takes precedence whenever the browser connection returns. The mini stays off limits.","body":{"conditions":"Reviewed packet lands on main: the chosen Worker and why, its configuration with a placeholder register, the parser check, and the planner procedure with rollback. Nothing deployed by the builder.","target_head":"2883992093b5b2ea54a220dea7f81da0f34cee44","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}